{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/770245-maniac-son-of-phobos","id":770245,"title":"Maniac Son of Phobos","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-20T13:23:48-08:00","id":770245,"title":"Maniac Son of Phobos","content":"So, I wasn't sure whether this should go here, or mage, or hunter, or what, but I've been working on this character for a while, and would love some feedback on him. My initial idea was of a Genius, or Maniac, slasher. Hannibal Lecter and Jigsaw, and others like them, always fascinated me. Moriarty from the recent Sherlock Holmes movies I thought was awesome, in as much as he was just as brilliant and interesting as Sherlock himself, only totally self-serving. I was originally ST'ing a game for a bunch of characters we had pulled out of the then new Immortals book. Every gaming session took place twenty years after the last one. We started in the eighteen hundreds, we went ahead into a post-apocalyptic world. I had an Eternal that had a relic collection, one of those reincarnating characters, a Purified that used to be a promethean. It was all pretty cool. Anyway, my bad guy was a Maniac blood bather. At the time, I only used blood bathing because it was so adaptable, and I didn't have anything better. Anyway, we finished that campaign, but the character has haunted me as being awesome, and I wanted a chance to play him wherever I went. As you can imagine, not a lot of people are into slasher characters to start with, let alone with one that needed to kill in gruesome ways to maintain any kind of immortality. <br /> <br /> Then Blood Sorcery came out, and I was ecstatic: Sons of Phobos. This was the perfect fit for my Maniac character. I liked the idea of him using his intelligence and his longevity as his biggest weapons. Someone so smart, so long-lived, could have incredibly Byzantine and convoluted plans that required decades or centuries to complete. I loved the idea of him being able to use his divination blood magic with his genius and maniac gifts to get the better of people he hadn't even met. But there was another element here, and that was the mad doctor. Somehow, ever since his first incarnation, he was a doctor, he was a surgeon. It made sense, when you needed to harvest a person's blood to live forever. I had him working as a surgeon for patchwork people, the obscenely rich and powerfully influential. It gave him clout, and strings with which he could enact his plans. For his clients, he was a patchwork surgeon, for his grunts, he was a thaumatech surgeon. Once he actually needed people's hearts for his immortality, it only made more sense for him to be a surgeon. With the sons of phobos, there is an alternate rule that makes his minions become masks, if the character sacrifices a whole dot of WP. A mask under the direction of a maniac? Awesome! And the ability to replace that super-minion's body parts with more dangerous ones from monsters you've collected? Awesome! Imagine a Jason type character that could regenerate like a werewolf, with a berserker splice. It took me a long, long time, but I did gather the synergy of the merit murder expert with the thaumatech implant hand of glory. Giving my guy those two and weapon monomaniac seemed to make sense. I mean, he uses the same knife for all his procedures, it's almost a part of him, now. <br /> <br /> His original purpose was to use the rite of hecate to steal a gnosis of 5, and then use long forgotten rituals to kickstart his own archmage event. He desperately felt like he deserved all that power, and was frustrated that it was never something he could just have. So, I've obviously put a lot of thought into this guy over the years. I would love to hear people's responses, feedback, anything. How can he be improved? What would you use a character like this for, how would you handle him, how would you oppose him, in character, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9514-sunforger42","name":"Sunforger42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T23:50:10-08:00","id":772125,"title":"","content":"Honestly, he can be improved by some serious streamlining here, he's all over the place to a rather silly extent, and would pretty much lose absolutely nothing if you just fully used options. <br /> <br /> Son of phobos makes being a chiron surgeon and a promethean brother pretty much useless. His magic is just as versatile as witchcraft, and he can use transformation to give his minions abilities, or just flat out make minions. <br /> <br /> Or you could make him a witch, and just give him mysteries to prolong his own life and sacrifice people for source, two very in theme abilities for a witch. Want minons as a witch? Make zombies, or summon spirits/ghosts/demons.<br /> <br /> Want slasher minions, summon spirits/demons/ghosts and have them urge people until they become serial killers. Or just cut out the middle man and summon a spirit of murder and put it into someone or a spare corpse. <br /> <br /> Patchwork surgeon? He has magic, if he needs an actual job for money and connections he's doing it wrong. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}